"Discussiones Mathematicae (https://www.dmgt.uz.zgora.pl/publish/pdf.php?doi=2572)\nciteturn2search12 [wordlim: 200] Published: last year; NEIGHBOR-LOCATING CHROMATIC NUMBER ... In the paper (Discussiones Mathematicae Graph Theory 43 (2023) 659–\n675) has been posed two conjectures on neighbor-locating coloring of graphs.\nDiscussiones Mathematicae\nGraph Theory xx (xxxx) 1–9\nhttps://doi.org/10.7151/dmgt.2572\nON TWO CONJECTURES REGARDING THE\nNEIGHBOR-LOCATING CHROMATIC NUMBER\nAli Ghanbari 1\nDepartment of Mathematics\nFaculty of Mathematical Sciences\nUniversity of Mazandaran\nBabolsar, Iran\ne-mail: ali.ghanbari239@gmail.com\nand\nDoost Ali Mojdeh 2\nDepartment of Mathematics\nFaculty of Mathematical Sciences\nUniversity of Mazandaran\nBabolsar, Iran\ne-mail: damojdeh@umz.ac.ir\nAbstract\nIn the paper (Discussiones Mathematicae Graph Theory 43 (2023) 659–\n675) has been posed two conjectures on neighbor-locating coloring of graphs.\nIn this paper, we disprove one of them by presenting a family of counterex-\namples and prove the another one.\nKeywords: coloring, neighbor-locating coloring, conjectures.\n2020 Mathematics Subject Classification: 05C15, 05C76.\n1.\nIntroduction\nLet G = (V, E) be a simple, finite, connected and undirected graph, with the set\nof vertices V = V (G) and the set of edges E = E(G). The open neighborhood\nof a vertex v in G, denoted by NG(v) = N(v), is the set of vertices adjacent to\n1ORCID: 0009-0005-5875-4838.\n2Corresponding author, ORCID: 0000-0001-9373-3390.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEstimating the Koebe radius for polynomials (https://arxiv.org/abs/1805.06927)\nciteturn2academia13 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.5 years ago; Title: Estimating the Koebe radius for polynomials ... For a pair of conjugate trigonometrical polynomials $C (t) = \\sum_ { j = 1 } ^N { { a_j}\\cos jt }, S(t) = \\sum_ { j = 1 } ^N { { a_j}\\sin jt }$ with real coefficients and normalization ${a_1} = 1 $ we solve the extremal problem \\[ \\sup_ {a_2,...,a_N} \\left ({ \\min_t \\left\\{ {\\Re \\left ({ F\\left ({ { e^ {it} } } \\right) } \\right): \\Im \\left ({ F\\left ({ { e^ {it} } } \\right) } \\right) = 0 } \\right\\} } \\right) = -\\frac14 \\sec ^2\\frac\\pi{N + 2}.\nTitle: Estimating the Koebe radius for polynomials\nAuthors: Dmitriy Dmitrishin, Andrey Smorodin, Alex Stokolos\nDate: Thu May 17 19:00:16 2018\n\nFor a pair of conjugate trigonometrical polynomials $C (t) = \\sum_ { j = 1 } ^N { { a_j}\\cos jt }, S(t) = \\sum_ { j = 1 } ^N { { a_j}\\sin jt }$ with real coefficients and normalization ${a_1} = 1 $ we solve the extremal problem \\[ \\sup_ {a_2,...,a_N} \\left ({ \\min_t \\left\\{ {\\Re \\left ({ F\\left ({ { e^ {it} } } \\right) } \\right): \\Im \\left ({ F\\left ({ { e^ {it} } } \\right) } \\right) = 0 } \\right\\} } \\right) = -\\frac14 \\sec ^2\\frac\\pi{N + 2}. \\] We show that the solution is unique and is given by \\[ a_j^ {(0)} = \\frac {1} { { { U'_N}\\left ({\\cos \\frac{\\pi } { { N + 2 } } } \\right) } } { U' _ { N - j + 1 } }\\left ({\\cos \\frac{\\pi } { { N + 2 } } } \\right) { U_ { j - 1 } }\\left ({\\cos \\frac{\\pi } { { N + 2 } } } \\right), \\] where the $U_j(x)$ are the Chebyshev polynomials of the second kind, and the $U'_j(x)$ are their derivatives, $j = 1, \\ldots, N.$ As a consequence, we obtain some theorems on covering of intervals by polynomial images of the unit disc. We formulate several conjectures on a number of extremal problems on classes of polynomials.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\ndblp: On two conjectures regarding the neighbor-locating chromatic number. (https://dblp.dagstuhl.de/rec/journals/dmgt/GhanbariM25.html)\nciteturn2search0 [wordlim: 200] Crawled: 2 months ago; # \"On two conjectures regarding the neighbor-locating chromatic number.\"\n\n# \"On two conjectures regarding the neighbor-locating chromatic number.\"\n\n  * help us\n\n    * How can I correct errors in dblp?\n    * contact dblp\n\nAli Ghanbari, Doost Ali Mojdeh (2025)\n\n\n## Details and statistics\n\n  * show external API response\n\n    * JSON @ openalex.org\n\nsee also:\n\n    * API doc @ openalex.org\n\nDOI: 10.7151/DMGT.2572\n\n\nmetadata version: 2026-05-07\n\n  * Image: Journal Articles\n\n    * view\n\n      * electronic edition via DOI (open access)\n\nauthority control:\n\n      * BibTeX\n      * RIS\n      * RDF N-Triples\n      * RDF Turtle\n      * RDF/XML\n      * XML\n      * plain text\n\ndblp key:\n\n      * journals/dmgt/GhanbariM25\n\n\n      * https://dblp.org/rec/journals/dmgt/GhanbariM25\n\nAli Ghanbari, Doost Ali MojdehImage: 0000-0001-9373-3390:\nOn two conjectures regarding the neighbor-locating chromatic number. Discuss. Math. Graph Theory 45(4): 1095-1103 (2025)\n\n\nlast updated on 2026-05-07 20:24 CEST by the dblp team\n\n all metadata released as open data under CC0 1.0 license--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nNEIGHBOR LOCATING COLORING ON THE PRODUCT OF GRAPHS (https://gcgt.ug.edu.pl/wp-content/uploads/2024/06/Mojdeh.pdf)\nciteturn2search14 [wordlim: 200] Published: 2.4 years ago; A \\(k\\)-coloring \\(\\pi=\\{S_1,\\cdots,S_k\\}\\) of \\(V(G)\\) is a neighbor-locating coloring if any two vertices \\(u,v\\in S_i\\), there is a color class \\(S_j\\) for which, one of them has a neighbor in \\(S_j\\) and the other not. ... Disccussions Mathematicae Graph Theory, 43 (2023) 659–675, https://doi.org/10.7151/dmgt.2392. ... On the conjectures of neighbor locating coloring of graphs.\nNEIGHBOR LOCATING COLORING ON THE PRODUCT OF GRAPHS\n\nDoost Ali Mojdeh\n\nDepartment of Mathematics, Faculty of Mathematical Sciences,  \nUniversity of Mazandaran  \ne-mail: damojdeh@umz.ac.ir\n\nAli Ghanbari\n\nDepartment of Mathematics, Faculty of Mathematical Sciences,  \nUniversity of Mazandaran  \ne-mail: ali.ghanbari239@gmail.com\n\nLet \\(G\\) be a graph. A \\(k\\)-coloring of \\(G\\) is a partition \\(\\pi=\\{S_1,\\cdots,S_k\\}\\) of \\(V(G)\\) so that each \\(S_i\\) are independent set and take same color. A \\(k\\)-coloring \\(\\pi=\\{S_1,\\cdots,S_k\\}\\) of \\(V(G)\\) is a neighbor-locating coloring if any two vertices \\(u,v\\in S_i\\), there is a color class \\(S_j\\) for which, one of them has a neighbor in \\(S_j\\) and the other not. The minimum \\(k\\) with this property, is said to be neighbor-locating chromatic number of \\(G\\), denote by \\(\\chi_{NL}(G)\\) of \\(G\\).  \nIn this talk we discuss on the neighbor-locating chromatic number of Cartesian and lexicographic product of two graphs.\n\nReferences\n\n[1] L. Alcon, M. Gutierrez, C. Hernando, M. Mora and I.M. Pelayo, Neighbor-locating colorings in graphs, Theoretical Computer Science, 806, (2020) 144–155.\n\n[2] L. Alcon, M. Gutierrez, C. Hernando, M. Mora, and I. M. Pelayo, The neighbor-locating-chromatic number of pseudotrees, arXiv:1903.11937v1 [math.CO] 28 Mar (2019).\n\n[3] L. Alcon, M. Gutierrez, C. Hernando, M. Mora and I.M. Pelayo, The neighbor-locating-chromatic number of trees and unicyclic graphs. Disccussions Mathematicae Graph Theory, 43 (2023) 659–675, https://doi.org/10.7151/dmgt.2392.\n\n[4] D. A. Mojdeh. On the conjectures of neighbor locating coloring of graphs. Theoretical Computer Science, 922 (2022) 300–307.--------------------------------------------------------------------------------\nEstimating the Koebe radius for polynomials (https://www.researchgate.net/publication/325262669_Estimating_the_Koebe_radius_for_polynomials)\nciteturn2search1 [wordlim: 200] Published: 8.5 years ago; Crawled: 5 months ago; ESTIMATING THE KOEBE RADIUS FOR POLYNOMIALS 9 ... Note that we cannot apply the Riemann Theorem and the Lindel¨of ... Indeed, for even N the image of D under the univalent polynomial map ... For odd N, on the contrary, the radius equals |F(e iτ N)|, ... Finally, let us note that a right hand of the estimate (20) monoton- ... favor of Conjecture 1. ... tion